## Approach

Three position-only correction functions in a new `src/corrections.rs`. Per the task description, speed correction is NOT handled by these functions — the caller (pipeline in swisseph-rs/30) applies finite-difference speed correction externally. This differs from the C architecture where each function handles its own speed, but produces the same final result when the pipeline applies the right intervals.

Golden test strategy: `meff` and `aberr_light` tested by calling C functions directly with synthetic inputs (both are non-global, pure-parameter functions). `deflect_light` tested via swe_calc pipeline comparison (the C function accesses global state, making direct calls impractical from a test harness).

